00:54:16.899 --> 00:54:19.269
This one's from Avery.
这是来自艾弗里的。

00:54:20.440 --> 00:54:26.989
Dear Craig and Josh, I want to start by taking you back to season two, episode 17, Areva Deirci Fierro.
亲爱的克雷格和乔什，我想首先带你们回到第二季第 17 集，Areva Deirci Fierro。

00:54:26.989 --> 00:54:35.699
In that episode, we learned how a beat-up old Fierro became the vehicle literally and and figuratively for Ted and Marshall's friendship.
在那一集中，我们了解了一个破旧的老费罗如何成为泰德和马歇尔友谊的载体。

00:54:35.699 --> 00:54:42.340
Those road trips, singing along to, I'm gonna be 500 miles, created a bond that transcended the miles traveled.
那些公路旅行，伴随着“我要行驶 500 英里”的歌声，建立了一种超越里程的纽带。

00:54:42.340 --> 00:54:47.539
I'm writing to you because my own life has a red Mustang version of that story.
我写信给你是因为我自己的生活中也有这个故事的红色野马版本。

00:54:47.539 --> 00:54:55.380
During my undergrad years at Marquette University in Milwaukee, my best friend Jake and I took countless road trips in his red Mustang.
在密尔沃基马凯特大学读本科期间，我和我最好的朋友杰克开着他的红色野马进行了无数次公路旅行。

00:54:55.380 --> 00:55:02.539
Like Ted and Marshall in the Fierro, those drives became our sacred space, the place where a friendship transformed into brotherhood.
就像菲耶罗的特德和马歇尔一样，这些驱动器成为我们的神圣空间，在这里友谊转化为兄弟情谊。

00:55:02.539 --> 00:55:09.860
And on those trips, windows down and the road stretching out before us, we bonded over our mutual love for how I met your mother.
在那些旅行中，车窗摇下，道路在我们面前延伸，我们因对我与你母亲的相识而彼此相爱，从而将我们联系在一起。

00:55:09.860 --> 00:55:13.539
I came to Marquette carrying the weight of a difficult family situation.
我带着困难的家庭状况来到马凯特。

00:55:13.539 --> 00:55:19.579
Your show arrived in my life at exactly the right moment, offering something I desperately needed, a roadmap.
你的节目在正确的时刻出现在我的生活中，提供了我迫切需要的东西，一个路线图。

00:55:19.579 --> 00:55:28.380
You taught me that family isn't just who you're born to, it's the people you choose, the ones who show up for you and your best times and stand beside you through your worst.
你教会了我，家庭不仅是你出生的人，也是你选择的人，是那些在你最好的时候出现在你身边、在你最糟糕的时候陪伴你的人。

00:55:28.380 --> 00:55:34.099
The gang at McLarens wasn't just a friend group, they were proof that you could build your own family.
迈凯伦的团队不仅仅是一个朋友团体，他们证明了你可以建立自己的家庭。

00:55:34.099 --> 00:55:39.940
Jake became my brother and through him I found my own gang, a group of friends who were still my family to this day.
杰克成了我的兄弟，通过他我找到了自己的帮派，一群朋友，直到今天仍然是我的家人。

00:55:39.940 --> 00:55:44.579
We lived and breathed the show, we suited up, we accepted challenges.
我们生活在这场演出中，我们穿好衣服，我们接受挑战。

00:55:44.579 --> 00:55:55.000
How I met your mother wasn't just something we watched, it became the language through which we understood friendship, love and what it means to really show up for each other.
我如何遇见你母亲不仅仅是我们观看的事情，它还成为我们理解友谊、爱情以及真正为彼此展现意义的语言。

00:55:55.000 --> 00:56:00.719
A few years after we graduated, I called Jake after my first date with a woman named Andrea.
我们毕业几年后，我在与一位名叫安德里亚的女人第一次约会后给杰克打了电话。

00:56:00.719 --> 00:56:05.519
We'd met at a cocktail lounge, ordered drinks and appetizers and talked for hours, and then it happened.
我们在鸡尾酒吧见面，点了饮料和开胃菜，聊了几个小时，然后事情就发生了。

00:56:05.519 --> 00:56:15.159
The olive theory right there on our first date, our appetizers arrived and without thinking she immediately reached for the olives while I instinctively pushed them aside.
橄榄理论就在我们第一次约会时，我们的开胃菜上来了，她不假思索地立即伸手去拿橄榄，而我本能地将它们推到一边。

00:56:15.159 --> 00:56:19.360
We both stopped, looked at each other and laughed because we both knew what that meant.
我们都停下来，互相看着对方，笑了，因为我们都知道这意味着什么。

00:56:19.360 --> 00:56:24.960
It was such a small moment, but in that instant I knew I told Jake right then she was the one.
那是一个很小的时刻，但在那一刻，我知道我当时就告诉了杰克，她就是那个人。

00:56:24.960 --> 00:56:41.199
Your show became part of Andrea's and my love story from that very first date and earlier this year when we got married, Jake stood up as my best man and said, Andrea, to quote Avery's favorite show, How I Met Your Mother, You Pass the Front Porch Test.
从第一次约会开始，你的节目就成为安德里亚和我爱情故事的一部分，今年早些时候，当我们结婚时，杰克作为我的伴郎站起来说，安德里亚，引用了艾弗里最喜欢的节目《老爸老妈的浪漫史》，你通过了前廊测试。

00:56:41.199 --> 00:56:46.519
I'll see you guys on the porch in 50 years for our daily match of bridge.
50 年后我会在门廊上见到你们，参加我们每天的桥牌比赛。

00:56:46.519 --> 00:56:49.960
But beyond the laughs and the catchphrases your show taught me something profound.
但除了笑声和流行语之外，你的节目还教会了我一些深刻的东西。

00:56:49.960 --> 00:56:58.119
It's okay to be vulnerable, it's okay to feel, it's okay to fail, because the best things in life are worth waiting for.
脆弱没关系，感受也没关系，失败也没关系，因为生命中最好的事情都值得等待。

00:56:58.119 --> 00:57:05.119
Looking back now, I'm grateful for every heartbreak, every hardship, every wrong turn, because they all led me to Andrea.
现在回想起来，我很感激每一次心碎、每一次艰难、每一次错误的转折，因为它们都引导我找到了安德里亚。

00:57:05.119 --> 00:57:10.079
They led me to the life I'm living now, married to the woman of my dreams.
他们带领我过上了现在的生活，嫁给了我梦想中的女人。

00:57:10.079 --> 00:57:20.759
Now listening to how we made your mother, and hearing the behind the scenes stories of how you crafted these moments, I'm reminded all over again of the intentionality and heart you poured into every episode.
现在，听着我们如何塑造你的母亲，听着你如何创造这些时刻的幕后故事，我再次想起你在每一集里倾注的意图和心血。

00:57:20.759 --> 00:57:23.840
It's been such a gift to revisit the show through your eyes.
通过你的眼睛重温这部剧真是一份礼物。

00:57:23.840 --> 00:57:28.009
Thank you for creating something that became so much more than entertainment.
感谢您创造了不仅仅是娱乐的东西。

00:57:28.009 --> 00:57:34.235
Thank you for giving someone navigating a difficult family situation, a vision of what shows and family looks like.
感谢您为某人提供了解决家庭困难的机会，让他们了解了节目和家庭的情况。

00:57:34.235 --> 00:57:43.440
Thank you for the laughter, the tears and the belief that our stories, no matter how meandering, are leading us exactly where we need to be with immense gratitude, Avery.
谢谢你的欢笑、泪水，并相信我们的故事，无论多么曲折，都会怀着巨大的感激之情引导我们到达我们需要去的地方，艾弗里。

00:57:43.440 --> 00:57:44.139
Fantastic.
极好的。

00:57:44.139 --> 00:57:47.076
It's so cool how this show has turned out.
这个节目的结果真是太酷了。

00:57:47.076 --> 00:57:52.811
The show about love has turned out to be a part of so many real-life love stories.
这部关于爱情的节目已经成为许多现实生活爱情故事的一部分。

00:57:52.811 --> 00:57:54.000
It's really cool.
真的很酷。

00:57:55.119 --> 00:58:02.153
I was thinking about this that we can talk about this if we talk about this more as the years go on.
我在想，如果随着时间的推移我们能更多地谈论这个问题，我们就可以讨论这个问题。

00:58:02.153 --> 00:58:10.803
We talked about there was something about Ted that felt a little out of fashion or a little bit out of step with the times.
我们谈到泰德身上有一些感觉有点不合时宜，或者有点与时代格格不入。

00:58:10.803 --> 00:58:14.250
It was still like a real dudes, dudes on the air.
它仍然像一个真正的花花公子，在广播中的花花公子。

00:58:14.250 --> 00:58:29.230
And I always was like, I know I'm playing this very vulnerable guy who leads with his heart on the sleeve, his vulnerable feelings, but he's got this emotional resilience that I found to be very heroic and strong.
我总是想，我知道我扮演的是一个非常脆弱的人，他的心在袖子上，他的脆弱的感情，但他有这种情感上的韧性，我发现这是非常英勇和坚强的。

00:58:29.230 --> 00:58:32.676
But it's so wonderful to hear a letter like that.
但听到这样的信真是太好了。

00:58:32.676 --> 00:58:36.193
He taught me it's okay to feel, it's okay to fail.
他告诉我，感受也没关系，失败也没关系。

00:58:36.193 --> 00:58:50.329
And that's That's why I think Ted and the show as a whole has aged pretty well, you know, there was some real, I don't know, there was just a feeling of like, like, stop, stop with this vulnerable guy.
这就是为什么我认为特德和整个节目已经很好地老化了，你知道，有一些真实的，我不知道，只是有一种感觉，就像，停止，停止与这个脆弱的家伙在一起。

00:58:50.329 --> 00:58:54.150
You guys even got notes from the network, like, you know, who would be like this?
你们甚至从网络上得到了笔记，比如，你知道，谁会是这样的？

00:58:54.150 --> 00:59:07.190
And you're like, we're like this, you know, but it's just so nice to have it reflected back that our gamble on a character like this and paid off in ages as well because it's It's true.
你会说，我们就是这样的，你知道，但很高兴能反映出我们对这样一个角色的赌博，并在很长一段时间内得到了回报，因为这是真的。

00:59:07.190 --> 00:59:08.190
Yeah.
是的。

00:59:08.190 --> 00:59:15.429
It's the truth of how people are and how men are, you know, it's the pretending otherwise that seems to cause all the problems.
这就是人性和人性的真相，你知道，假装的样子似乎造成了所有的问题。

00:59:15.429 --> 00:59:16.429
Yeah.
是的。

00:59:16.429 --> 00:59:17.429
Yeah.
是的。

00:59:17.429 --> 00:59:18.429
Well, thanks, Avery.
嗯，谢谢，艾弗里。

00:59:18.429 --> 00:59:19.429
Thanks, Ross.
谢谢，罗斯。

00:59:19.429 --> 00:59:20.429
We just loved reading those letters.
我们只是喜欢读这些信。

00:59:20.429 --> 00:59:21.429
Yeah.
是的。

00:59:21.429 --> 00:59:22.429
That's great.
那太棒了。

00:59:22.429 --> 00:59:23.429
We love talking.
我们喜欢说话。

00:59:23.429 --> 00:59:24.429
I love talking about this episode.
我喜欢谈论这一集。

00:59:24.429 --> 00:59:25.429
This was really fun, Craig.
这真的很有趣，克雷格。

00:59:25.429 --> 00:59:26.429
Yeah.
是的。

00:59:26.429 --> 00:59:27.429
So this is a great one.
所以这是一件很棒的事情。

00:59:27.429 --> 00:59:28.429
Go Chris Harris.
去吧，克里斯·哈里斯。

00:59:28.429 --> 00:59:29.429
Go everybody.
大家都去吧。

00:59:29.429 --> 00:59:30.429
Everybody was firing on all cylinders except the Fierro.
除了 Fierro 之外，每个人都在全力以赴。

00:59:30.429 --> 00:59:31.429
Boom.
繁荣。

00:59:31.429 --> 00:59:33.429
And that's how you end an episode.
这就是结束一集的方式。

00:59:33.429 --> 00:59:34.429
I am guilty.
我有罪。

